IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg3-stock-issue`
IMPORT `dg3-capital-dividends`
IMPORT `dg3-own-stock`
IMPORT `dg3-subscriptions`
IMPORT `dg3-certificates`
IMPORT `dg3-transfers`
IMPORT `dg3-s203`
IMPORT `dg3-seat`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: sections 151 to 174 and 201 to 203 -- WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT QUESTIONS.
--
-- One or more cases for every question in dg3-seat.l4, in the order of that file. Each case is a person in a stated situation; the expected value was decided by reading
-- the section the question cites and is written beside the assertion, not copied from the output. A yes/no question is asserted TRUE or FALSE; a question the text may leave
-- unanswered is asserted JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING; a number is asserted to the dollar or the share.
-- The text file is a converter rendering, not the official text: each expected value is a reading of that rendering.

§ `Section 151: classes and series, redemption, conversion, designations`

-- Q1. A founder asks whether the terms of the preferred stock may be fixed in the certificate of incorporation: yes.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The board fixes them by resolution under authority the certificate expressly gives it: yes.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in a resolution of the board of directors` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The board fixes them by resolution, but the certificate gives it no such authority: no.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in a resolution of the board of directors` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A conversion price tied to an outside index, with nothing said about how the index operates: no.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The same, but the certificate says clearly how the index operates: yes.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The terms are in the bylaws: section 151(a) names only the certificate and a board resolution, so no.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in the bylaws` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The terms are nowhere written down: no.
#ASSERT `May the terms of the class or series be fixed this way` `in none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q2. A founder asks whether a determination by a third-party appraiser is a fact: the text says a fact includes an event, a determination or action by any person or body.
#ASSERT `Is the matter a fact for the terms of a class or series` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Something that is neither an event nor a determination or action: the text says "includes, but is not limited to", so it does not say it is not a fact.
#ASSERT `Is the matter a fact for the terms of a class or series` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q3. A holder of Series A stock asks whether the power to increase or decrease the capital stock reaches that series: it does, if the series is of a class the corporation may issue under 151(a).
#ASSERT `Does the power to adjust the capital stock apply to my class or series` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the power to adjust the capital stock apply to my class or series` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q4. A holder of redeemable preferred stock, where the company will have common shares with full voting power outstanding after the redemption: allowed, at the corporation's option.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made subject to redemption` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Redeemable at the holders' option, but after the redemption no share with full voting power would remain: not allowed under the proviso.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made subject to redemption` `at the option of the holders of the stock under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The same, for the stock of a registered investment company redeemable at the holders' option: paragraph (b)(1) lifts the proviso.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made subject to redemption` `at the option of the holders of the stock under s 151(b)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The same company, but the stock is to be redeemed on a specified event: paragraph (b)(1) names only redemption at the option of the corporation or of the holders, so the proviso still applies and the answer is no.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made subject to redemption` `upon the happening of a specified event under s 151(b)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A broadcaster whose licence depends on its holders' qualifications, redeeming only as far as needed to keep the licence: allowed even with no voting shares left.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made subject to redemption` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The same broadcaster, but redeeming more than needed to keep the licence: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made subject to redemption` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q5. The redemption price and dates are in the certificate: valid.
#ASSERT `Are the redemption price and times of my stock validly stated` `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- They are in a board resolution under express authority: valid.
#ASSERT `Are the redemption price and times of my stock validly stated` `in a resolution of the board of directors` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- They are in a board resolution without express authority in the certificate: not valid.
#ASSERT `Are the redemption price and times of my stock validly stated` `in a resolution of the board of directors` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- They are only in the bylaws: not valid.
#ASSERT `Are the redemption price and times of my stock validly stated` `in the bylaws` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q6. A holder of preferred stock whose dividend rate is stated in the certificate: entitled as stated.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to dividends on my preferred or special stock as stated` TRUE `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The holder of common stock asks the same: section 151(c) speaks of preferred or special stock, so no.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to dividends on my preferred or special stock as stated` FALSE `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Preferred stock whose dividend terms are in a board resolution that the certificate did not authorise: no.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to dividends on my preferred or special stock as stated` TRUE `in a resolution of the board of directors` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Preferred stock whose dividend terms are in a resolution under express authority: yes.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to dividends on my preferred or special stock as stated` TRUE `in a resolution of the board of directors` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q7. The preferred dividends have been paid or set apart and assets are available: a dividend may now be paid on the common.
#ASSERT `May a dividend now be paid on the remaining classes or series` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The preferred dividend has not been paid or set apart: not yet.
#ASSERT `May a dividend now be paid on the remaining classes or series` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The preferred dividend is provided for but no assets are available for dividends: no.
#ASSERT `May a dividend now be paid on the remaining classes or series` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q8. A holder of preferred stock whose rights on liquidation are in the certificate: entitled as stated.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the stated rights on dissolution or distribution of assets` TRUE `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A holder of common stock: section 151(d) speaks of preferred or special stock, so no.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the stated rights on dissolution or distribution of assets` FALSE `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Liquidation rights in the bylaws: no.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the stated rights on dissolution or distribution of assets` TRUE `in the bylaws` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q9. Series B is convertible into common stock of the same corporation, on terms in the certificate: allowed.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made convertible or exchangeable` TRUE `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Convertible into the shares of a different company: section 151(e) speaks of other classes or series of the corporation's own stock, so no.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made convertible or exchangeable` FALSE `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Convertible into another class of its own stock, but the terms are in a board resolution without authority: no.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made convertible or exchangeable` TRUE `in a resolution of the board of directors` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The same under express authority: yes.
#ASSERT `May stock like mine be made convertible or exchangeable` TRUE `in a resolution of the board of directors` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q10. A corporation that may issue common and preferred, whose certificate summarises each class's rights on the certificate: complies.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate state the rights of each class and series as the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Its certificates instead carry a statement that the rights will be furnished free on request: complies.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate state the rights of each class and series as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- It does neither: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate state the rights of each class and series as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The statement-on-request route is closed where section 202 provides otherwise (a restriction on transfer): does not comply.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate state the rights of each class and series as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- A corporation with one class and no series has nothing to state under this sentence: complies.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate state the rights of each class and series as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q11. A holder of uncertificated shares got a written notice, in a reasonable time, with the certificate information and the class-rights statement: complies.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I received for my uncertificated stock what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The notice was oral: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I received for my uncertificated stock what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The notice came a year late: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I received for my uncertificated stock what the Law requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The notice left out the transfer-restriction legend: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I received for my uncertificated stock what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The notice left out the class rights and any statement that they will be furnished: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Was the notice I received for my uncertificated stock what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q12. A holder of uncertificated shares of the same class as certificated shares, no law providing otherwise: same rights and obligations.
#ASSERT `Do I have the same rights and obligations as a holder of a certificate of the same class and series` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Where another provision of law expressly provides otherwise: not the same.
#ASSERT `Do I have the same rights and obligations as a holder of a certificate of the same class and series` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q13. The terms of a new series are in a board resolution under express authority and are not in the certificate: a certificate of designations is required before issuing.
#ASSERT `Must our corporation file a certificate of designations before issuing shares of this class or series` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The terms are already set forth in the certificate: none required.
#ASSERT `Must our corporation file a certificate of designations before issuing shares of this class or series` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The terms are in the certificate, and a board resolution adds nothing: none required.
#ASSERT `Must our corporation file a certificate of designations before issuing shares of this class or series` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q14. Terms in a board resolution, not in the certificate, and the certificate of designations is filed and effective: requirement met.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation met the requirement of a certificate of designations` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The same, but not yet filed: not met.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation met the requirement of a certificate of designations` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Terms are in the certificate itself: nothing was required, so met without a filing.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation met the requirement of a certificate of designations` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q15. Series A has 100 shares of a 200-share class and 80 outstanding; the board resolved to raise it to 150 and a certificate to that effect is filed: allowed.
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` FALSE 100 150 200 80 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Raising it to 250 would exceed the 200 authorised for the class: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` FALSE 100 250 200 80 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lowering it to 70 would go below the 80 outstanding: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` FALSE 100 70 200 80 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lowering it to exactly the 80 outstanding is allowed (the bound is "not below").
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` FALSE 100 80 200 80 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Raising it to exactly the 200 authorised for the class is allowed (the bound is "not above").
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` FALSE 100 200 200 80 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No certificate stating the board's authorisation has been filed: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` FALSE 100 150 200 80 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board's resolution otherwise provides ("unless otherwise provided in any such resolution"): the text does not say what then.
#ASSERT `May the number of shares of our series be changed by certificate` TRUE 100 150 200 80 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q16. Series A is cut from 100 to 60 shares: the 40 shares resume the status they had before the first resolution.
#ASSERT `How many shares resume their earlier status when our series is decreased` 100 60 EQUALS 40
-- A change from 100 to 150 is not a decrease: none resume.
#ASSERT `How many shares resume their earlier status when our series is decreased` 100 150 EQUALS 0

-- Q17. No Series C shares were ever issued, the board resolved so, and the elimination certificate is filed and effective: the designations are eliminated.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate eliminate the matters set forth in the certificate of designations` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Shares are still outstanding: not eliminated.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate eliminate the matters set forth in the certificate of designations` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The elimination certificate has not become effective: not eliminated.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate eliminate the matters set forth in the certificate of designations` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q18. A series set up by board resolution, with no shares issued and nothing in the certificate to the contrary: the board may amend its terms by resolution.
#ASSERT `May our board amend the terms of a class or series by resolution before any share is issued` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Some shares have been issued: no.
#ASSERT `May our board amend the terms of a class or series by resolution before any share is issued` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The series was set out in the certificate itself and not by board resolution: no.
#ASSERT `May our board amend the terms of a class or series by resolution before any share is issued` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The certificate provides otherwise: no.
#ASSERT `May our board amend the terms of a class or series by resolution before any share is issued` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q19. A certificate of amendment states that none have been issued, sets forth the resolution, and the designation is unchanged: it has the required contents.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment have the contents the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The designation is being renamed and the certificate gives the old and the new: required contents.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment have the contents the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The designation is being renamed but the certificate does not indicate the old and new: lacks them.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment have the contents the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- It does not state that no shares have been issued: lacks them.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment have the contents the Law requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- It does not set forth a copy of the resolution: lacks them.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment have the contents the Law requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q20. The certificate has the contents and is filed and effective: it amends the certificate of incorporation.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment amend the certificate of incorporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Filed but missing required contents: it does not amend.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment amend the certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Has the contents but is not yet effective: it does not amend.
#ASSERT `Does our certificate of amendment amend the certificate of incorporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q21. The board has authority under 151(g) and a restated certificate has since been filed: it may still adopt such resolutions.
#ASSERT `May our board still adopt such resolutions after a certificate or a restated certificate has been filed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A board with no such authority: it may not.
#ASSERT `May our board still adopt such resolutions after a certificate or a restated certificate has been filed` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Sections 152 to 158: issuing stock, consideration, capital, fractions, partly paid shares, rights and options, certificates`

-- Q22. The board's resolution sets out numbers, times and consideration, and the consideration is cash: authorised.
#ASSERT `Has our board authorised the issue of stock for this consideration` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A resolution accepting a patent licence (intangible property) as the consideration: authorised.
#ASSERT `Has our board authorised the issue of stock for this consideration` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A resolution accepting a benefit to the corporation (a founder's past services): authorised.
#ASSERT `Has our board authorised the issue of stock for this consideration` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Cash, but there is no board resolution: not authorised.
#ASSERT `Has our board authorised the issue of stock for this consideration` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Nothing of the four kinds is given for the shares: not authorised.
#ASSERT `Has our board authorised the issue of stock for this consideration` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q23. A board delegating to its CEO the power to issue stock, fixing a maximum, a period and a minimum consideration, and not letting her issue to herself: allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of stock to a person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- No maximum number of shares fixed: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of stock to a person or body` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- No time period fixed: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of stock to a person or body` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- No minimum consideration fixed: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of stock to a person or body` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The resolution lets her issue stock to herself: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of stock to a person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q24. Delegation: at most 1,000 shares, between 1 Jan and 31 Dec 2026, at not less than 500; 400 already issued; now 300 shares on 15 Jun 2026 for 500, not to the delegate: within it.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) 500 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 600 shares would bring the total to exactly 1,000: still within.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 600 (YMD 2026 6 15) 500 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 601 shares would bring the total to 1,001: over the maximum.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 601 (YMD 2026 6 15) 500 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Issued on the last day of the period, 31 Dec 2026: within.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 300 (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Issued on 1 Jan 2027, after the period: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 300 (YMD 2027 1 1) 500 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Issued on 31 Dec 2025, before the period: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 300 (YMD 2025 12 31) 500 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- For 499, below the minimum of 500: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) 499 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Issued to the delegate itself: outside, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `Is this issue within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue stock` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) 500 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) 500 TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q25. A resolution to issue stock makes the price depend on a published index, and says how the index operates: allowed.
#ASSERT `May a provision of our board's resolution depend on facts outside the resolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The same, but the resolution does not say how the index operates: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May a provision of our board's resolution depend on facts outside the resolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A provision that depends on nothing outside the resolution: nothing to forbid.
#ASSERT `May a provision of our board's resolution depend on facts outside the resolution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q26. A determination by the board's own committee: the text counts a determination or action as a fact.
#ASSERT `Is the matter a fact for a resolution under section 152` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Something that is neither an event nor a determination or action: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Is the matter a fact for a resolution under section 152` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q27. A delegating resolution under which the maximum number of shares depends on what the delegate determines: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May the limits fixed for the delegate depend on the delegate's own determination or action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- A delegating resolution whose limits do not depend on the delegate: allowed.
#ASSERT `May the limits fixed for the delegate depend on the delegate's own determination or action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A resolution that does not delegate: the restriction is not engaged.
#ASSERT `May the limits fixed for the delegate depend on the delegate's own determination or action` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q28. A director asks whether the board's valuation of a patent licence stands: conclusive, there being no actual fraud.
#ASSERT `Is the directors' judgment of the value of the consideration conclusive` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- With actual fraud in the transaction: not conclusive.
#ASSERT `Is the directors' judgment of the value of the consideration conclusive` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q29. A stockholder whose shares were issued in accordance with section 152 and fully paid for: fully paid and nonassessable.
#ASSERT `Is my stock fully paid and nonassessable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The consideration has not yet been received: not yet.
#ASSERT `Is my stock fully paid and nonassessable` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Partly paid shares under section 156: no.
#ASSERT `Is my stock fully paid and nonassessable` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not issued in accordance with section 152: no.
#ASSERT `Is my stock fully paid and nonassessable` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Sections 153 and 154: consideration for stock, capital, surplus and net assets`

-- Q30. 100 shares of $10 par: the board fixed a minimum of $1,000, exactly the aggregate par: enough.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum consideration our board fixed at least what section 153 requires` 1000 TRUE 10 100 EQUALS TRUE
-- A minimum of $999: not enough.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum consideration our board fixed at least what section 153 requires` 999 TRUE 10 100 EQUALS FALSE
-- Shares without par value, a minimum of $1: the Law requires nothing, so enough.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum consideration our board fixed at least what section 153 requires` 1 FALSE 0 100 EQUALS TRUE

-- Q31. 100 shares of $10 par need consideration worth at least $1,000.
#ASSERT `What consideration does section 153 require for these shares` TRUE 10 100 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Shares without par value: the section requires no consideration at all ("if any"), so there is no amount to give.
#ASSERT `What consideration does section 153 require for these shares` FALSE 0 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q32. Par shares, aggregate par $1,000, board-determined consideration worth $1,000: allowed.
#ASSERT `May shares with a par value be issued for this consideration` 1000 1000 `the board of directors under s 152` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Worth $999: below par, so no.
#ASSERT `May shares with a par value be issued for this consideration` 999 1000 `the board of directors under s 152` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The stockholders determined it, and the certificate so provides: allowed.
#ASSERT `May shares with a par value be issued for this consideration` 1500 1000 `the stockholders under s 153` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The stockholders determined it but the certificate does not reserve that right to them: no.
#ASSERT `May shares with a par value be issued for this consideration` 1500 1000 `the stockholders under s 153` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q33. No-par shares for consideration the board determined: allowed.
#ASSERT `May shares without par value be issued for this consideration` `the board of directors under s 152` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The stockholders determined it under a certificate that so provides: allowed.
#ASSERT `May shares without par value be issued for this consideration` `the stockholders under s 153` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The stockholders determined it, the certificate silent: no.
#ASSERT `May shares without par value be issued for this consideration` `the stockholders under s 153` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q34. Treasury shares sold in the way that shares are issued: allowed.
#ASSERT `May treasury shares be disposed of in this way` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Treasury shares sold for consideration the stockholders determined, the certificate so providing: allowed.
#ASSERT `May treasury shares be disposed of in this way` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Neither route: no.
#ASSERT `May treasury shares be disposed of in this way` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The stockholders determined it, the certificate silent: no.
#ASSERT `May treasury shares be disposed of in this way` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q35. The certificate requires only the default majority: 51 of 100 votes outstanding carry it.
#ASSERT `Have the stockholders validly determined the consideration for the shares` FALSE 0 51 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 50 of 100 is not a majority (more than half).
#ASSERT `Have the stockholders validly determined the consideration for the shares` FALSE 0 50 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The certificate requires two thirds: 67 of 100 carry it.
#ASSERT `Have the stockholders validly determined the consideration for the shares` TRUE (200 DIVIDED BY 3) 67 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 66 of 100 does not reach two thirds.
#ASSERT `Have the stockholders validly determined the consideration for the shares` TRUE (200 DIVIDED BY 3) 66 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The certificate requires 75%: exactly 75 of 100 reaches it.
#ASSERT `Have the stockholders validly determined the consideration for the shares` TRUE 75 75 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q36. $1,000 received for shares of $100 aggregate par, all with par, for cash, and the board set $500 as capital at issue: capital is $500.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 500 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST 500
-- The board set exactly the aggregate par ($100), which is enough where all the shares have par.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 100 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST 100
-- The board made no determination: capital is the aggregate par, $100.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST 100
-- Mixed par and no-par shares ($400 for the no-par ones) and no determination: par plus the no-par consideration, $500.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 400 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE 0 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST 500
-- Mixed shares, and the board set $300, which is in excess of the aggregate par: capital is $300.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 400 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 300 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST 300
-- Mixed shares and the board set only $100, equal to par but not in excess of it: the Law requires "in excess of" for mixed issues, and does not say what the capital is when the board falls short.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 400 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 100 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- All the shares have par and the board set $50, below the aggregate par of $100: also a determination the section does not permit, and it does not say what then.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 50 (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Shares for property (not cash), issued 1 Mar 2026, board determination on 30 Apr 2026, which is 60 days after the issue: in time.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 500 (YMD 2026 4 30) EQUALS JUST 500
-- The same on 1 May 2026, 61 days after: too late, so the default applies, $100.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 500 (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS JUST 100
-- Shares for cash, determination a day after the issue: the Law says "at the time of issue", so too late; $100.
#ASSERT `How much of the consideration for these shares is capital` 1000 100 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE 500 (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS JUST 100

-- Q37. The board designated $400 as capital for the no-par shares: that is their stated capital.
#ASSERT `What is the stated capital of shares without par value` 400 EQUALS 400
-- The amount designated as capital for them is $0: their stated capital is $0.
#ASSERT `What is the stated capital of shares without par value` 0 EQUALS 0

-- Q38. Capital is $500, net assets $800 and the board directs $200 of net assets be transferred to capital: capital becomes $700.
#ASSERT `What would our capital be if the board transfers part of the net assets to the capital account` 500 800 200 EQUALS JUST 700
-- The transfer may take all the excess of net assets over capital, $300.
#ASSERT `What would our capital be if the board transfers part of the net assets to the capital account` 500 800 300 EQUALS JUST 800
-- A transfer of $301 exceeds the net assets in excess of capital: the Law does not allow it.
#ASSERT `What would our capital be if the board transfers part of the net assets to the capital account` 500 800 301 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q39. Total assets $1,000 and liabilities $400 (not counting capital and surplus): net assets $600.
#ASSERT `What are the net assets of our corporation` 1000 400 EQUALS 600
-- Total assets equal to total liabilities: net assets are zero.
#ASSERT `What are the net assets of our corporation` 500 500 EQUALS 0

-- Q40. Net assets $600 and capital $500: surplus $100.
#ASSERT `What is the surplus of our corporation, if any` 1000 400 500 EQUALS JUST 100
-- Capital equal to the net assets: no excess, so no surplus.
#ASSERT `What is the surplus of our corporation, if any` 1000 400 600 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q41. A stock corporation's capital is what section 154 works out, $500.
#ASSERT `What is the capital of our corporation for sections 154, 160 and 170` `a stock corporation` 500 EQUALS 500
-- A nonstock corporation's capital is deemed to be zero.
#ASSERT `What is the capital of our corporation for sections 154, 160 and 170` `a charitable nonstock corporation` 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the capital of our corporation for sections 154, 160 and 170` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` 500 EQUALS 0

§ `Sections 155 and 156: fractions of shares; partly paid shares`

-- Q42. A corporation that issues fractions of a share has nothing further to arrange.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation dealt with fractional interests as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A corporation that does not issue fractions and pays the fair value in cash, $100 for $100: complies.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation dealt with fractional interests as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE 100 100 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- It paid $50 for fractions worth $100: not the fair value, so does not comply.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation dealt with fractional interests as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE 50 100 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- It issued scrip exchangeable for a full share: complies.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation dealt with fractional interests as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE 0 100 TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- It arranged for the disposition of the fractional interests by those entitled: complies.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation dealt with fractional interests as the Law requires` FALSE TRUE 0 100 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- It does none of the three: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Has our corporation dealt with fractional interests as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE 0 100 FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q43. A holder of a certificate for a fractional share asks whether it votes: yes.
#ASSERT `Can I exercise this right with my fractional interest` `a certificate for a fractional share under s 155` `the right to exercise voting rights under s 155` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A holder of an uncertificated fractional share asks about the right to a share of the assets on liquidation: yes.
#ASSERT `Can I exercise this right with my fractional interest` `an uncertificated fractional share under s 155` `the right to participate in the assets of the corporation in the event of liquidation under s 155` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A holder of scrip asks whether it carries dividends, the scrip being silent: no.
#ASSERT `Can I exercise this right with my fractional interest` `scrip or warrants under s 155` `the right to receive dividends under s 155` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The scrip itself provides that it carries voting rights: yes.
#ASSERT `Can I exercise this right with my fractional interest` `scrip or warrants under s 155` `the right to exercise voting rights under s 155` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q44. Scrip that becomes void if not exchanged before 1 Jun 2026, exchanged for full shares on 31 May 2026: not void.
#ASSERT `Have my scrip or warrants become void` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 5 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Exchanged on 1 Jun 2026 itself: not "before" that date, so void.
#ASSERT `Have my scrip or warrants become void` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Never exchanged: void under the condition.
#ASSERT `Have my scrip or warrants become void` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- No such condition on the scrip: never void on that ground.
#ASSERT `Have my scrip or warrants become void` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q45. Our corporation issues scrip in lieu of fractions; the board may make it void if not exchanged before a date.
#ASSERT `May our board cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to this condition` TRUE `that they become void if not exchanged for full shares before a specified date under s 155` EQUALS TRUE
-- It may provide that the shares for which the scrip is exchangeable are sold and the proceeds distributed to the holders.
#ASSERT `May our board cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to this condition` TRUE `that the shares for which they are exchangeable may be sold and the proceeds distributed to the holders under s 155` EQUALS TRUE
-- Any other condition the board imposes: the text sets no limit.
#ASSERT `May our board cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to this condition` TRUE `any other condition which the board of directors may impose under s 155` EQUALS TRUE
-- The corporation issues no scrip, but cash for fractions: there is no scrip to attach a condition to.
#ASSERT `May our board cause scrip or warrants to be issued subject to this condition` FALSE `any other condition which the board of directors may impose under s 155` EQUALS FALSE

-- Q46. A holder of a partly paid share whose certificate states the amounts: complies.
#ASSERT `Does my partly paid share carry the statement the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The certificate is silent: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Does my partly paid share carry the statement the Law requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Uncertificated shares whose amounts are in the corporation's books: complies.
#ASSERT `Does my partly paid share carry the statement the Law requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Uncertificated shares, nothing in the books: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Does my partly paid share carry the statement the Law requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q47. A $10 dividend on each fully paid share; my share is to be paid $100 in all and $60 is paid: I am entitled to $6.
#ASSERT `What dividend am I entitled to on a partly paid share` 10 100 60 EQUALS JUST 6
-- A share that is fully paid ($100 of $100): the whole $10.
#ASSERT `What dividend am I entitled to on a partly paid share` 10 100 100 EQUALS JUST 10
-- A share for which nothing has been paid: nothing.
#ASSERT `What dividend am I entitled to on a partly paid share` 10 100 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A total consideration of zero has no percentage paid: the text gives no answer.
#ASSERT `What dividend am I entitled to on a partly paid share` 10 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 157: rights and options`

-- Q48. A corporation whose certificate does not forbid rights or options: may create and issue them.
#ASSERT `May our corporation create and issue rights or options to acquire its stock` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Its certificate forbids them: may not.
#ASSERT `May our corporation create and issue rights or options to acquire its stock` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q49. A board resolution sets out numbers, times and consideration and the terms of exercise are in the certificate: as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Are our rights or options issued and their terms stated as the Law requires` TRUE `in the certificate of incorporation` EQUALS TRUE
-- The terms of exercise are in a board resolution: as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Are our rights or options issued and their terms stated as the Law requires` TRUE `in a resolution of the board of directors` EQUALS TRUE
-- The terms of exercise are only in the bylaws: not as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Are our rights or options issued and their terms stated as the Law requires` TRUE `in the bylaws` EQUALS FALSE
-- No board resolution: not as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Are our rights or options issued and their terms stated as the Law requires` FALSE `in the certificate of incorporation` EQUALS FALSE

-- Q50. A delegation of the issue of options fixing the maximum, the periods and the minimum, and barring self-issue: allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of rights or options to a person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- No maximum number of shares: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of rights or options to a person or body` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- No time periods: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of rights or options to a person or body` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The delegate may issue options to itself: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May our board delegate the issue of rights or options to a person or body` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q51. Delegation: up to 1,000 shares on exercise; options issued during 2026; shares issued on exercise up to 31 Dec 2030; $10 minimum per option and $5 for the shares;
-- 400 already covered; this issue covers 300 shares; options issued 15 Jun 2026 for $10; shares to be issued 15 Jun 2028 for $5; not to the delegate: within it.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 6 15) 10 5 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Exactly 1,000 in all (400 + 600): still within.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 600 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 6 15) 10 5 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 1,001 in all: over the maximum.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 601 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 6 15) 10 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Options issued 1 Jan 2027, after the period for issuing options: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 300 (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2028 6 15) 10 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Shares to be issued on exercise on 1 Jan 2031, after the period for the shares: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2031 1 1) 10 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Options sold for $9, below the $10 minimum: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 6 15) 9 5 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Exercise price $4, below the $5 minimum for the shares: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 6 15) 10 4 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Options issued to the delegate itself: outside.
#ASSERT `Is this issue of rights or options within the resolution that delegated the authority to issue them` 1000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE 10 5 400 300 (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 6 15) 10 5 TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q52. A resolution to issue options makes the exercise price depend on an outside index and says how it operates: allowed.
#ASSERT `May a provision of our board's resolution on rights or options depend on facts outside the resolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Without saying how: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May a provision of our board's resolution on rights or options depend on facts outside the resolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q53. An action by a person or body is a fact for section 157; something else the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Is the matter a fact for a resolution under section 157` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the matter a fact for a resolution under section 157` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q54. A delegation whose limits depend on the delegate's own determination: not allowed.
#ASSERT `May the limits fixed for the delegate of rights or options depend on the delegate's own determination or action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `May the limits fixed for the delegate of rights or options depend on the delegate's own determination or action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q55. Options over 100 shares of $10 par with a minimum exercise consideration of $1,000: enough.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum consideration for shares issued on exercise at least what section 153 requires` 1000 TRUE 10 100 EQUALS TRUE
-- A minimum of $999: not enough.
#ASSERT `Is the minimum consideration for shares issued on exercise at least what section 153 requires` 999 TRUE 10 100 EQUALS FALSE

§ `Sections 158 and 159: certificates, uncertificated shares, personal property`

-- Q56. The board resolved that the class is uncertificated and my shares were never certificated: uncertificated.
#ASSERT `Are my shares uncertificated shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- My shares are still represented by a certificate I have not surrendered: the resolution does not yet reach them.
#ASSERT `Are my shares uncertificated shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- I surrendered the certificate: uncertificated.
#ASSERT `Are my shares uncertificated shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- No board resolution: shares are represented by certificates.
#ASSERT `Are my shares uncertificated shares` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q57. A holder of stock represented by certificates is entitled to a certificate.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a stock certificate` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a stock certificate` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q58. A certificate signed by two authorised officers: as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Is my certificate signed as the Law requires` 2 EQUALS TRUE
-- Signed by one officer: not.
#ASSERT `Is my certificate signed as the Law requires` 1 EQUALS FALSE
-- Signed by three: the Law asks for any 2, and three is at least two.
#ASSERT `Is my certificate signed as the Law requires` 3 EQUALS TRUE

-- Q59. A certificate in bearer form: the corporation has no power to issue it.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation power to issue a certificate in bearer form` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- A registered certificate: the bar on bearer certificates does not touch it.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation power to issue a certificate in bearer form` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q60. Shares of stock are personal property.
#ASSERT `Are my shares of stock personal property` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are my shares of stock personal property` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q61. A transfer made as Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 provides: the shares are transferable by it.
#ASSERT `Are my shares transferable by this transfer` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are my shares transferable by this transfer` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q62. A nonresident holder of stock of a Delaware corporation: exempt from Delaware taxation under section 159.
#ASSERT `Is my stock or are my bonds exempt from taxation by Delaware` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A foreign corporation holder: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my stock or are my bonds exempt from taxation by Delaware` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A Delaware resident: the sentence does not say the stock is taxed, only when it is not.
#ASSERT `Is my stock or are my bonds exempt from taxation by Delaware` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Stock of a company not organised under this chapter: the sentence does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Is my stock or are my bonds exempt from taxation by Delaware` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q63. A transfer for collateral security which both transferor and transferee ask to be so expressed: it must be expressed in the entry.
#ASSERT `Must the entry of transfer say that the transfer is for collateral security` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Only one of them asks: not required.
#ASSERT `Must the entry of transfer say that the transfer is for collateral security` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- An absolute transfer: not required.
#ASSERT `Must the entry of transfer say that the transfer is for collateral security` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Sections 159 to 169: own stock, additional stock, unpaid stock, subscriptions, lost certificates, situs`

-- Q64. A stock corporation with capital intact and not impaired by this buy-back: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Its capital is already impaired: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Its capital is sound but the purchase would impair it: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Capital impaired, but the shares bought carry a preference on distribution of assets: the exception lets it buy out of capital.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Capital impaired, no preference shares outstanding, the shares retired on acquisition and the capital reduced under sections 243 and 244: allowed.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The same, but the capital is not reduced: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Preference shares are outstanding and the shares bought are not preference shares: the second limb is closed, so barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A nonstock corporation has no exception: barred even for a preference.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying or redeeming its own shares for cash or other property` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q65. A note given for bought shares when capital was sound and was not impaired by the note: still valid.
#ASSERT `Is a note or debenture our corporation gave for shares it bought still valid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Capital was already impaired when the note was delivered, but the note did not make it worse: the Law's words are "was not then impaired OR did not thereby become impaired", so the saving still applies.
#ASSERT `Is a note or debenture our corporation gave for shares it bought still valid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Capital was sound when the note was delivered, though the note itself then impaired it: the first limb is met, so the saving applies.
#ASSERT `Is a note or debenture our corporation gave for shares it bought still valid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Capital was already impaired and the note impaired it further: neither limb is met, so the saving does not apply.
#ASSERT `Is a note or debenture our corporation gave for shares it bought still valid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q66. Shares redeemable at the corporation's option at $100; it would pay $120: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying shares redeemable at its option for more than the redemption price` TRUE 120 100 EQUALS TRUE
-- It would pay exactly $100: not "more", so not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying shares redeemable at its option for more than the redemption price` TRUE 100 100 EQUALS FALSE
-- It would pay $99: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying shares redeemable at its option for more than the redemption price` TRUE 99 100 EQUALS FALSE
-- Shares not redeemable at the corporation's option: this bar does not reach them.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from buying shares redeemable at its option for more than the redemption price` FALSE 120 100 EQUALS FALSE

-- Q67. A stock corporation redeeming stock that section 151(b) allows (full voting shares remain) and following the certificate: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from redeeming these shares or membership interests` `a stock corporation` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The same, but no full-voting share would remain and no exception applies: 151(b) does not authorise it, so barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from redeeming these shares or membership interests` `a stock corporation` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Authorised by 151(b) but the redemption does not follow the certificate: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from redeeming these shares or membership interests` `a stock corporation` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A nonstock corporation whose certificate authorises redeeming membership interests and the redemption follows it: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from redeeming these shares or membership interests` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The certificate does not authorise it: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from redeeming these shares or membership interests` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Authorised, but not carried out in accordance with the certificate: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from redeeming these shares or membership interests` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` `at the option of the corporation under s 151(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q68. Shares bought out of surplus, not retired and not required to be: may be resold.
#ASSERT `May our corporation still resell shares it bought or redeemed out of surplus` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Already retired: no.
#ASSERT `May our corporation still resell shares it bought or redeemed out of surplus` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The certificate requires them to be retired: no.
#ASSERT `May our corporation still resell shares it bought or redeemed out of surplus` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Bought out of capital, not surplus: the saving does not reach them.
#ASSERT `May our corporation still resell shares it bought or redeemed out of surplus` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q69. Shares of our stock that we hold ourselves: not voted.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `the corporation itself under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Our own stock held by us as a fiduciary: the Law does not limit the right to vote it.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `the corporation itself under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Our stock held by another corporation of which we hold a majority of the shares entitled to vote for directors: not voted.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `another corporation under s 160(c)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Held by another corporation of which we hold only a minority: the section does not bar it, and does not say it may be voted.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `another corporation under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Held by a partnership in which we hold a majority of the voting power: not voted.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `any other entity under s 160(c)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Held by an entity we otherwise control: not voted.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `any other entity under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Held by a stranger to us: the section does not touch it.
#ASSERT `Can shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls be voted` `a holder that is neither the corporation, a corporation it controls nor an entity it controls under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q70. The same holders, for quorum: our own shares are not counted.
#ASSERT `Do shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls count toward a quorum` `the corporation itself under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Our own stock that we hold in a fiduciary capacity: the closing clause preserves the right to vote it and speaks of voting only; the text neither restores the shares to the quorum count nor says they stay out of it.
#ASSERT `Do shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls count toward a quorum` `the corporation itself under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Held by an entity we control through a majority of the voting power: not counted.
#ASSERT `Do shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls count toward a quorum` `any other entity under s 160(c)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Held by a stranger: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `Do shares held by the corporation or by an entity it controls count toward a quorum` `a holder that is neither the corporation, a corporation it controls nor an entity it controls under s 160(c)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q71. Notice of redemption sent on 1 May 2026 and the redemption sum irrevocably set aside on 10 May 2026: on 9 May the shares are still outstanding.
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 5 9) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) EQUALS TRUE
-- On 10 May, the day both conditions are met, they are no longer outstanding.
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 5 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) EQUALS FALSE
-- On a later day: still not outstanding.
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) EQUALS FALSE
-- The sum was set aside first (1 May) and the notice sent later (10 May): on 9 May still outstanding, on 10 May not.
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 5 9) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 5 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- No notice was sent: outstanding.
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 10) EQUALS TRUE
-- No sum was set aside: outstanding.
#ASSERT `Are my shares called for redemption still outstanding for voting on this day` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 5 10) EQUALS TRUE

-- Q72. The certificate authorises 1,000 shares, 900 are issued, subscribed for or committed: the directors may issue 100 more.
#ASSERT `May our directors issue or take subscriptions for additional shares` 1000 900 100 EQUALS TRUE
-- 101 more would go beyond the amount authorised.
#ASSERT `May our directors issue or take subscriptions for additional shares` 1000 900 101 EQUALS FALSE

-- Q73. A stockholder who owes the unpaid balance of the consideration, the corporation's assets being insufficient for its creditors: bound to pay.
#ASSERT `Am I bound to pay the unpaid balance on my shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The consideration has been paid in full: not bound.
#ASSERT `Am I bound to pay the unpaid balance on my shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The assets suffice for the creditors' claims: not bound.
#ASSERT `Am I bound to pay the unpaid balance on my shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q74. 100 shares with $5 unpaid on each: $500 to complete.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay to complete the unpaid balance on my shares` 100 5 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much must I pay to complete the unpaid balance on my shares` 0 5 EQUALS 0

-- Q75. Bound under 162(a) and a writ of execution against the corporation was returned unsatisfied: recoverable as section 325 provides.
#ASSERT `Can the amount I owe be recovered from me as section 325 provides` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- No writ returned unsatisfied yet: not yet.
#ASSERT `Can the amount I owe be recovered from me as section 325 provides` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not bound at all: no.
#ASSERT `Can the amount I owe be recovered from me as section 325 provides` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q76. A transferee who took in good faith and without notice that the consideration was unpaid: free of liability.
#ASSERT `Am I free of personal liability for the unpaid portion as an assignee or transferee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- One who knew: not free.
#ASSERT `Am I free of personal liability for the unpaid portion as an assignee or transferee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- One who did not act in good faith: not free.
#ASSERT `Am I free of personal liability for the unpaid portion as an assignee or transferee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q77. The transferee is not liable: the transferor remains liable.
#ASSERT `Does the transferor remain liable for the unpaid portion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The transferee is liable: the sentence says nothing about the transferor.
#ASSERT `Does the transferor remain liable for the unpaid portion` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q78. A person holding shares as collateral security is not personally liable as a stockholder.
#ASSERT `Am I personally liable as a stockholder` `as collateral security under s 162(d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An executor, trustee or other fiduciary is not personally liable.
#ASSERT `Am I personally liable as a stockholder` `as an executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary under s 162(d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A holder in another capacity: subsection (d) does not say.
#ASSERT `Am I personally liable as a stockholder` `in another capacity under s 162(d)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q79. The person who pledged the shares to me is the holder and liable.
#ASSERT `Is the person who pledged the shares to me considered the holder and liable` `as collateral security under s 162(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the person who pledged the shares to me considered the holder and liable` `in another capacity under s 162(d)` EQUALS FALSE

-- Q80. The estate or funds I hold as a fiduciary are liable.
#ASSERT `Are the estate or funds I hold as a fiduciary liable for the shares` `as an executor, administrator, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary under s 162(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the estate or funds I hold as a fiduciary liable for the shares` `as collateral security under s 162(d)` EQUALS FALSE

-- Q81. Stock issued 1 Mar 2020: liability asserted on 1 Mar 2026, exactly 6 years after, is not "more than 6 years" after, so it can still be asserted.
#ASSERT `Can liability on my shares or subscription still be asserted against me` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Asserted on 2 Mar 2026: more than 6 years after.
#ASSERT `Can liability on my shares or subscription still be asserted against me` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q82. A stockholder of an insolvent corporation in an action by its receiver for an assessment: may appear and contest.
#ASSERT `May I appear and contest a claim to assess me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The action is not for an assessment under section 162: no right under this subsection.
#ASSERT `May I appear and contest a claim to assess me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a stockholder or subscriber: no.
#ASSERT `May I appear and contest a claim to assess me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q83. The board judges the business requires $400 on each share on which $500 is unpaid: it may demand.
#ASSERT `May our directors demand this payment on stock that is not fully paid` TRUE 400 500 EQUALS TRUE
-- It may demand the whole balance, $500 ("not exceeding in the whole").
#ASSERT `May our directors demand this payment on stock that is not fully paid` TRUE 500 500 EQUALS TRUE
-- $501 exceeds the balance: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors demand this payment on stock that is not fully paid` TRUE 501 500 EQUALS FALSE
-- The board does not judge the business to require it: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors demand this payment on stock that is not fully paid` FALSE 400 500 EQUALS FALSE

-- Q84. Notice given 1 May 2026 for a payment on 31 May 2026, 30 days later, stating time and place, to every holder at the last known address: as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the payment I was given what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Payment on 30 May: only 29 days' notice.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the payment I was given what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 30) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The notice does not state the time and place: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the payment I was given what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- It was not given to every holder at the last known address: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the payment I was given what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q85. I failed to pay a call when due: the corporation may sue me or sell my shares at public sale.
#ASSERT `Can the corporation sue me or sell my shares at public sale because I did not pay a call` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the corporation sue me or sell my shares at public sale because I did not pay a call` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q86. Sale on 30 Jun 2026, advertised on 23 Jun (1 week before) in a newspaper of the registered office's county, notice mailed on 10 Jun (20 days before): as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the sale of my shares what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 23) (YMD 2026 6 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Advertised on 24 Jun, only 6 days before: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the sale of my shares what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 24) (YMD 2026 6 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Mailed on 11 Jun, only 19 days before: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the sale of my shares what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 23) (YMD 2026 6 11) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The notice does not state time, place and the sum due on each share: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the sale of my shares what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 23) (YMD 2026 6 10) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The advertisement ran in a newspaper of another county: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the sale of my shares what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 23) (YMD 2026 6 10) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The notice was not mailed to the last known post-office address: no.
#ASSERT `Is the notice of the sale of my shares what the Law requires` (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 23) (YMD 2026 6 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q87. No bidder; an action at law was brought on 15 Jan 2026; the amount was not collected; asked as of 16 Jan 2027, more than a year after: forfeited.
#ASSERT `Are my stock and the amount I paid in forfeited to the corporation` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2027 1 16) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Asked as of 15 Jan 2027, exactly a year after, the year is still running: not yet forfeited.
#ASSERT `Are my stock and the amount I paid in forfeited to the corporation` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2027 1 15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The amount was collected by the action on 1 Dec 2026, within the year: not forfeited.
#ASSERT `Are my stock and the amount I paid in forfeited to the corporation` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2027 2 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Collected only on 1 Mar 2027, after the year: forfeited as of 1 Jun 2027.
#ASSERT `Are my stock and the amount I paid in forfeited to the corporation` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A bidder could be had: no forfeiture.
#ASSERT `Are my stock and the amount I paid in forfeited to the corporation` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2027 2 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Q88. A preincorporation subscription dated 1 Jan 2026, terms silent, nobody consenting: irrevocable on 15 Jun 2026, within the 6 months.
#ASSERT `Is my preincorporation subscription irrevocable on the day I want to revoke it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 15 Jul 2026, after the 6 months: revocable.
#ASSERT `Is my preincorporation subscription irrevocable on the day I want to revoke it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 7 15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- All the other subscribers consent: revocable even within the 6 months.
#ASSERT `Is my preincorporation subscription irrevocable on the day I want to revoke it` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The corporation consents: revocable.
#ASSERT `Is my preincorporation subscription irrevocable on the day I want to revoke it` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The terms of the subscription provide otherwise: revocable.
#ASSERT `Is my preincorporation subscription irrevocable on the day I want to revoke it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A subscription to stock of an existing corporation: section 165 does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `Is my preincorporation subscription irrevocable on the day I want to revoke it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q89. A subscription in writing signed by me: the corporation is not barred from enforcing it.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation barred from enforcing my subscription against me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- An oral subscription: barred.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation barred from enforcing my subscription against me` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- In writing but unsigned by me or my agent: barred.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation barred from enforcing my subscription against me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q90. A certificate the corporation issued, alleged lost: it may issue a replacement.
#ASSERT `May the corporation issue me a new certificate or uncertificated shares in place of the lost one` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not a certificate it issued: no.
#ASSERT `May the corporation issue me a new certificate or uncertificated shares in place of the lost one` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not alleged to be lost, stolen or destroyed: no.
#ASSERT `May the corporation issue me a new certificate or uncertificated shares in place of the lost one` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q91. I am the owner of the lost certificate: the corporation may require a bond.
#ASSERT `May the corporation require me to give a bond before it replaces my lost certificate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- I am neither owner nor legal representative: no.
#ASSERT `May the corporation require me to give a bond before it replaces my lost certificate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q92. The corporation refuses to replace a certificate it issued, alleged lost, and I am the owner: I may apply to the Court of Chancery.
#ASSERT `May I apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to show cause` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The corporation has not refused: no.
#ASSERT `May I apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to show cause` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- I am not the owner or the owner's representative: no.
#ASSERT `May I apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to show cause` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q93. A complaint naming the corporation, the number and date of the certificate (known to me), the shares and to whom issued, and the circumstances of the loss: as the Law requires.
#ASSERT `Does my complaint state what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The number and date of the certificate are not known or ascertainable, so the complaint need not state them.
#ASSERT `Does my complaint state what the Law requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The number and date are known but the complaint omits them: no.
#ASSERT `Does my complaint state what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The complaint omits the circumstances of the loss: no.
#ASSERT `Does my complaint state what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The complaint omits the corporation's name: no.
#ASSERT `Does my complaint state what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The complaint omits the shares and to whom they were issued: no.
#ASSERT `Does my complaint state what the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q94. My application is by a complaint that states what the Law requires: the court makes an order to show cause.
#ASSERT `Will the court make an order requiring the corporation to show cause` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the court make an order requiring the corporation to show cause` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q95. A copy of the complaint and order served on 10 May 2026 for a hearing designated for 15 May 2026, 5 days later: in time.
#ASSERT `Was a copy of my complaint and the order served on the corporation in time` (YMD 2026 5 10) (YMD 2026 5 15) EQUALS TRUE
-- Served on 11 May, only 4 days before: not in time.
#ASSERT `Was a copy of my complaint and the order served on the corporation in time` (YMD 2026 5 11) (YMD 2026 5 15) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q96. The court is satisfied that I own the shares and that the certificate was lost, and no sufficient cause was shown: it will order new shares or a certificate.
#ASSERT `Will the court order the corporation to issue and deliver new uncertificated shares or a new certificate to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not satisfied that I am the lawful owner: no.
#ASSERT `Will the court order the corporation to issue and deliver new uncertificated shares or a new certificate to me` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not satisfied that the certificate was lost: no.
#ASSERT `Will the court order the corporation to issue and deliver new uncertificated shares or a new certificate to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Sufficient cause was shown against it: no.
#ASSERT `Will the court order the corporation to issue and deliver new uncertificated shares or a new certificate to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q97. The court has ordered the corporation to issue new shares to me: I must give the bond first.
#ASSERT `Must I give the corporation a bond before the new shares or certificate are issued and delivered to me` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I give the corporation a bond before the new shares or certificate are issued and delivered to me` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q98. Shares issued under a court order, a claim of $5,000, a bond of $3,000: the corporation is liable for no more than $3,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the corporation can be made to pay on a claim after replacing a certificate under a court order` TRUE 5000 3000 EQUALS JUST 3000
-- A claim of $2,000: the corporation can be made to pay $2,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most the corporation can be made to pay on a claim after replacing a certificate under a court order` TRUE 2000 3000 EQUALS JUST 2000
-- Shares issued without a court order: the section sets no cap.
#ASSERT `What is the most the corporation can be made to pay on a claim after replacing a certificate under a court order` FALSE 5000 3000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q99. Stock of a Delaware corporation: its ownership is regarded as in Delaware for title, action, attachment, garnishment and jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `title under s 169` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `action under s 169` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `attachment under s 169` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `garnishment under s 169` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `jurisdiction of the courts held in this State under s 169` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not for the purpose of taxation.
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `taxation under s 169` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Some other purpose: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` TRUE `another purpose under s 169` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A corporation that does not exist under Delaware law: the section does not speak.
#ASSERT `Is the ownership of my stock regarded as located in Delaware for this purpose` FALSE `title under s 169` EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Sections 170 to 174 and 201 to 202: dividends, directors' liability, transfers and restrictions`

-- Q100. A stock corporation: assets $1,000, liabilities $400, capital $500, so net assets $600 and surplus $100. A $100 dividend is within the surplus: may be paid.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 100 1000 400 500 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- A $101 dividend exceeds the $100 surplus; with some surplus existing, (a)(2) is open only "in case there shall be no such surplus", so it may not be paid out of net profits either.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 101 1000 400 500 500 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- No surplus (net assets $500 equal capital $500) but net profits of $200 this year: a $150 dividend may be paid out of net profits.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 150 1000 500 500 200 0 300 EQUALS TRUE
-- The same, for $250, more than the $200 of net profits: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 250 1000 500 500 200 0 300 EQUALS FALSE
-- Net profits $100 this year and $150 last year: "for the fiscal year in which the dividend is declared and/or the preceding fiscal year", so $250 in all, and a $250 dividend may be paid.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 250 1000 500 500 100 150 300 EQUALS TRUE
-- $251 is one more than the two years' net profits: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 251 1000 500 500 100 150 300 EQUALS FALSE
-- No surplus and capital ($500) diminished below the capital of the preference stock ($600): no dividend out of net profits until the deficiency is repaired.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 100 1000 800 500 500 0 600 EQUALS FALSE
-- Exactly equal capital and preference capital ($500 each): not diminished below it, so the net-profits route is open.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 100 1000 500 500 500 0 500 EQUALS TRUE
-- The certificate forbids this dividend: no, whatever the surplus.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` FALSE 100 1000 400 500 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A $550 dividend with capital $500 would exceed the surplus of $100: no for a stock corporation.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a stock corporation` TRUE 550 1000 400 500 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- The same figures for a nonstock corporation, whose capital the Law deems to be zero: the surplus is the whole $600 of net assets, and $550 is within it.
#ASSERT `May our directors declare and pay this dividend` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` TRUE 550 1000 400 500 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE

-- Q101. A note paid as a dividend when the corporation had surplus or net profits to pay it lawfully: remains valid.
#ASSERT `Does a note or debenture paid as a dividend remain valid` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does a note or debenture paid as a dividend remain valid` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q102. A mining company whose certificate does not forbid it: its directors may ignore depletion in working out net profits.
#ASSERT `May our directors determine our net profits without taking depletion into consideration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A retailer, not exploiting wasting assets: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors determine our net profits without taking depletion into consideration` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A mining company whose certificate forbids it: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors determine our net profits without taking depletion into consideration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q103. The funds are available for dividends and the purpose is proper: a reserve may be set apart.
#ASSERT `May our directors set apart a reserve out of the funds available for dividends` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The funds are not available for dividends: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors set apart a reserve out of the funds available for dividends` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The purpose is not a proper one: no.
#ASSERT `May our directors set apart a reserve out of the funds available for dividends` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q104. A reserve set apart under section 171 may be abolished.
#ASSERT `May our directors abolish a reserve they set apart` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `May our directors abolish a reserve they set apart` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q105. A director who relied in good faith on the corporation's records about the value of its assets: fully protected, with no need to show expertise or selection.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `the records of the corporation under s 172` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A director who relied on a report from an officer: fully protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by an officer or employee under s 172` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A director who relied on a report from a committee of the board: fully protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by a committee of the board under s 172` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A director who relied on an outside appraiser reasonably believed to be expert and selected with reasonable care: fully protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by any other person under s 172` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The outside appraiser was not selected with reasonable care: not protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by any other person under s 172` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The director could not reasonably believe the matter within the outsider's expert competence: not protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `information, opinions, reports or statements presented by any other person under s 172` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The director did not rely in good faith: not protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE FALSE `the records of the corporation under s 172` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a member of the board or of a committee it designated: not protected by this section.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` FALSE TRUE `the records of the corporation under s 172` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The reliance was on a matter the section does not list (not the value of assets, liabilities or profits, or the funds for dividends or redemption): not protected.
#ASSERT `Am I fully protected for relying on what I relied on` TRUE TRUE `the records of the corporation under s 172` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q106. A dividend paid in cash in accordance with the chapter: may be paid.
#ASSERT `May our corporation pay this dividend in this form` TRUE `a dividend in cash under s 173` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May our corporation pay this dividend in this form` TRUE `a dividend in property under s 173` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May our corporation pay this dividend in this form` TRUE `a dividend in shares of the capital stock of the corporation under s 173` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A dividend in some other form: the section lists three forms and does not say about a fourth.
#ASSERT `May our corporation pay this dividend in this form` TRUE `a dividend in another form under s 173` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A cash dividend not in accordance with the chapter: no.
#ASSERT `May our corporation pay this dividend in this form` FALSE `a dividend in cash under s 173` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Q107. A stock dividend of $800 aggregate par, with $1,000 designated as capital by board resolution: the designation is not less than the par.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE 1000 800 FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Exactly $800: still not less than the aggregate par.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE 800 800 FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- $799: less than the par.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE 799 800 FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- No board resolution directing the designation: no.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` FALSE FALSE 1000 800 FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A split-up of the stock rather than a dividend: no designation is necessary.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` TRUE FALSE 0 800 FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Some shares are without par value and the board determined their amount: complies.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE 1000 800 TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Some shares are without par value and the board did not determine their amount: does not comply.
#ASSERT `Is the amount our board designated as capital for a dividend paid in shares what the Law requires` FALSE TRUE 1000 800 FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q108. A director under whose administration an unlawful dividend was paid on 1 Jan 2026, wilfully or negligently, sued by the corporation on 1 Jan 2032, exactly 6 years later, present and not dissenting: liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2032 1 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Sued on 2 Jan 2032, more than 6 years later: not liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2032 1 2) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The payment did not violate section 160 or 173: not liable under this section.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The violation was neither wilful nor negligent: not liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a director under whose administration it happened: not liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Dissented and had the dissent entered in the minutes: exonerated, so not liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Dissented but never had the dissent entered: not exonerated, liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q109. The same director, sued by a creditor of the corporation after its dissolution or insolvency: liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the creditors of the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The corporation is neither dissolved nor insolvent: creditors cannot sue under this section.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the creditors of the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Claim made 7 years later: out of time.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the creditors of the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2033 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Dissent entered: exonerated.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to the creditors of the corporation as a director for an unlawful dividend, stock purchase or redemption` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q110. A director absent when it was done who had the dissent entered on the minutes: exonerated.
#ASSERT `Am I exonerated from liability as a director because I was absent or dissented` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Absent but never had a dissent entered: not exonerated.
#ASSERT `Am I exonerated from liability as a director because I was absent or dissented` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Present and assenting: not exonerated.
#ASSERT `Am I exonerated from liability as a director because I was absent or dissented` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q111. $10,000 unlawfully paid with $500 interest: the directors are liable for $10,500.
#ASSERT `For how much are the directors liable for an unlawful dividend, purchase or redemption` 10000 500 EQUALS 10500
#ASSERT `For how much are the directors liable for an unlawful dividend, purchase or redemption` 10000 0 EQUALS 10000

-- Q112. A director against whom a claim was successfully asserted, asking contribution from a director who voted for the dividend: entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to contribution from the other director` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The other director did not vote for or concur in it: not entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to contribution from the other director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- No claim has been successfully asserted against me: not entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to contribution from the other director` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q113. A director paid $6,000 on a successful claim; I (a stockholder) received $2,000 of the $10,000 that stockholders with knowledge received: I can be made to repay $1,200, in proportion.
#ASSERT `How much can a director who paid a successful claim recover from me as a stockholder` TRUE 6000 TRUE 2000 10000 EQUALS JUST 1200
-- I received it without knowledge of facts indicating it was unlawful: subsection (c) gives the director no subrogation right against me, and says nothing of any other right, so the text gives no amount.
#ASSERT `How much can a director who paid a successful claim recover from me as a stockholder` TRUE 6000 FALSE 2000 10000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No claim has been successfully asserted against the director: subsection (c) is not engaged, so the text gives no amount.
#ASSERT `How much can a director who paid a successful claim recover from me as a stockholder` FALSE 6000 TRUE 2000 10000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No stockholder received it with knowledge (total zero) yet I say I did: the proportion is undefined.
#ASSERT `How much can a director who paid a successful claim recover from me as a stockholder` TRUE 6000 TRUE 2000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q114. Nothing in the chapter provides otherwise and nothing in it is inconsistent with Article 8: Article 8 governs the transfer.
#ASSERT `Which law governs the transfer of my stock` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 under s 201`
-- The chapter otherwise provides for the matter: the chapter governs.
#ASSERT `Which law governs the transfer of my stock` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `this chapter under s 201`
-- A provision of the chapter is inconsistent with one in subtitle I of Title 6: the chapter controls.
#ASSERT `Which law governs the transfer of my stock` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `this chapter under s 201`

-- Q115. A written restriction permitted by section 202, noted conspicuously on my certificate: enforceable against me.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Permitted but not noted on my certificate, and I have no actual knowledge: not enforceable.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not noted on the certificate, but I have actual knowledge of it: enforceable against me.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Uncertificated shares, with the restriction in the notice given under section 151(f): enforceable.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Uncertificated shares and the notice does not contain it: not enforceable without actual knowledge.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A restriction that is not written: not enforceable under this section.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- A restriction that section 202 does not permit: not enforceable.
#ASSERT `Can this restriction on my securities be enforced against me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q116. A restriction imposed by the certificate of incorporation, by the bylaws, by an agreement among holders, or by one among holders and the corporation: may be imposed.
#ASSERT `May a restriction on my securities be imposed in this way` `by the certificate of incorporation under s 202(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a restriction on my securities be imposed in this way` `by the bylaws under s 202(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a restriction on my securities be imposed in this way` `by an agreement among any number of security holders under s 202(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a restriction on my securities be imposed in this way` `by an agreement among such holders and the corporation under s 202(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other way: subsection (b) does not say.
#ASSERT `May a restriction on my securities be imposed in this way` `in another way under s 202(b)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q117. A restriction adopted after I got my securities, to which I am a party by an agreement: binding on me.
#ASSERT `Is a restriction adopted after I got my securities binding on me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I voted in favor of it: binding on me.
#ASSERT `Is a restriction adopted after I got my securities binding on me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am neither a party nor did I vote for it: not binding.
#ASSERT `Is a restriction adopted after I got my securities binding on me` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- My securities were issued after the restriction: the sentence does not speak to them.
#ASSERT `Is a restriction adopted after I got my securities binding on me` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q118. A right of first refusal exercisable within a reasonable time: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A right of first refusal exercisable only after an unreasonably long time: not permitted by that limb.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- An obligation to buy under a buy-sell agreement: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A requirement of the corporation's consent to transfers: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A drag-along that causes an automatic sale: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A bar on transfer to competitors, a designation that is not manifestly unreasonable: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A bar on transfer to a designation that is manifestly unreasonable: not permitted by that limb.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Any other lawful restriction: permitted by subsection (e).
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A restriction within none of the heads and not otherwise lawful: not permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this restriction on transfer or ownership permitted by section 202` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q119. A restriction that maintains subchapter S status: its purpose is conclusively presumed reasonable.
#ASSERT `Is the purpose of this restriction conclusively presumed to be reasonable` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the purpose of this restriction conclusively presumed to be reasonable` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the purpose of this restriction conclusively presumed to be reasonable` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the purpose of this restriction conclusively presumed to be reasonable` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the purpose of this restriction conclusively presumed to be reasonable` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A restriction with none of those purposes: the subsection does not say it is unreasonable, only that these are conclusively reasonable.
#ASSERT `Is the purpose of this restriction conclusively presumed to be reasonable` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Section 203(a): the three-year bar and its exceptions`

-- Q120. The board approved the business combination before I became an interested stockholder: yes.
#ASSERT `Did the board approve the business combination or the transaction before I became an interested stockholder` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Only the transaction that made me one was approved beforehand: yes.
#ASSERT `Did the board approve the business combination or the transaction before I became an interested stockholder` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Neither: no.
#ASSERT `Did the board approve the business combination or the transaction before I became an interested stockholder` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q121. I owned 90 of the 100 votes outstanding when the transaction commenced: at least 85%.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 90 100 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Exactly 85 of 100: at least 85%.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 85 100 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 84 of 100: not.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 84 100 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 77 of 120 votes outstanding, of which 20 are held by directors who are also officers and 10 by employee plans without a confidential tender decision: those 30 are left out of the base, 77 of 90 is 85.6%.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 77 120 20 0 10 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 76 of that base of 90 is 84.4%: not.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 76 120 20 0 10 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 5 of the officer-director votes are my own: they stay in the base ("but not the outstanding voting stock owned by the interested stockholder"), so 81 of 95.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 81 120 20 5 10 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No votes outstanding: no percentage.
#ASSERT `Did I own at least 85% of the voting stock outstanding when the transaction commenced` 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q122. The board approved the business combination at or after that time, it was authorised at a meeting and not by written consent, with 67 of the 100 votes not owned by me: yes.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE 67 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 66 of 100: not 66 2/3%.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE 66 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 200 of 300 is exactly 66 2/3%: yes.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE 200 300 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 199 of 300: no.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE 199 300 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board did not approve it: no.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE 90 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Authorised by written consent: the Law says "and not by written consent", so no.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE 90 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No votes outstanding that I do not own: no percentage.
#ASSERT `Was the business combination approved and authorized by the vote the Law requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q123. I became an interested stockholder on 1 Jan 2026; the business combination is on 1 Jun 2027; I own 20 of the 100 votes; the board approved nothing and no vote was taken: the corporation is barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The business combination is on 1 Jan 2029, the last day of the three years: still barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 2 Jan 2029, after the three years: not barred by this subsection.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 2) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board approved the business combination before I became an interested stockholder: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) TRUE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I owned 90% when the transaction ended: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) FALSE FALSE 90 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board approved at a later time and the stockholders authorised it at a meeting by 67 of the 80 votes I do not own (83.75%): not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE 67 80 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same vote of 50 of the 80 (62.5%): still barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in a business combination with me for 3 years after I became an interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE 50 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Section 203(b): when the restrictions do not apply`

-- Q124. The original certificate of incorporation expressly elects not to be governed by section 203: the restrictions do not apply.
#ASSERT `Did our original certificate of incorporation elect not to be governed by section 203` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did our original certificate of incorporation elect not to be governed by section 203` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q125. Our board adopted a bylaw amendment electing out on 1 Mar 1988, within 90 days of 2 Feb 1988: yes.
#ASSERT `Did our board elect out of section 203 by a bylaw amendment within 90 days of 2 February 1988` TRUE (YMD 1988 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- On 2 May 1988, the 90th day after 2 Feb 1988 (1988 was a leap year): still within.
#ASSERT `Did our board elect out of section 203 by a bylaw amendment within 90 days of 2 February 1988` TRUE (YMD 1988 5 2) EQUALS TRUE
-- On 3 May 1988, the 91st day: outside.
#ASSERT `Did our board elect out of section 203 by a bylaw amendment within 90 days of 2 February 1988` TRUE (YMD 1988 5 3) EQUALS FALSE
-- No such amendment: no.
#ASSERT `Did our board elect out of section 203 by a bylaw amendment within 90 days of 2 February 1988` FALSE (YMD 1988 3 1) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q126. A bylaw amendment the board adopted under (b)(2): the board may not further amend it.
#ASSERT `Is our board barred from further amending the bylaw amendment adopted under section 203(b)(2)` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is our board barred from further amending the bylaw amendment adopted under section 203(b)(2)` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q127. 51 of the 100 votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote adopted an amendment to the certificate, and no other law requires more: a majority.
#ASSERT `Did our stockholders adopt the amendment by the vote the Law requires` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 50 of 100 is not a majority.
#ASSERT `Did our stockholders adopt the amendment by the vote the Law requires` `the bylaws under s 203(b)(3)` 50 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another law requires 66 2/3%: 51 is not enough.
#ASSERT `Did our stockholders adopt the amendment by the vote the Law requires` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 TRUE ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another law requires 66 2/3%: 67 is enough.
#ASSERT `Did our stockholders adopt the amendment by the vote the Law requires` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 67 100 TRUE ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No outstanding votes entitled to vote: no basis for a majority.
#ASSERT `Did our stockholders adopt the amendment by the vote the Law requires` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 0 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q128. A company that has never had a listed or widely held class and has not elected to be governed: its election takes effect on the day of the amendment (1 Mar 2026).
#ASSERT `From what day does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 take effect` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Any other company: 12 months after.
#ASSERT `From what day does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 take effect` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- A company that has elected to be governed by section 203: 12 months after.
#ASSERT `From what day does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 take effect` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 1)

-- Q129. A private company (never listed or widely held, never elected in), stockholders' certificate amendment effective 1 Mar 2026 by 51 of 100 votes; business combination on 1 Jun 2026 with a person who became an interested stockholder on 1 Jan 2026: the election takes effect at once and the person is not excluded, so free of the restrictions.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- The same, but the business combination is on 1 Feb 2026, before the amendment takes effect: not yet free.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- A company with a listed class: the amendment takes effect 12 months later (1 Mar 2027), and a person who became an interested stockholder on or before 1 Mar 2026 is excluded: not free.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- A person who became one exactly on 1 Mar 2026, the day the certificate took effect: still "on or before", so excluded.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- A person who became one on 2 Mar 2026: not excluded, and the business combination (1 Jun 2027) is after the 12 months: free.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS TRUE
-- The same person, but the business combination is on 1 Feb 2027, before the 12 months run out: not yet free.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 51 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS FALSE
-- The vote was only 50 of 100: the election was never validly adopted, so not free.
#ASSERT `Does our stockholders' election not to be governed by section 203 free the corporation from the restrictions in this business combination` `the bylaws under s 203(b)(3)` 50 100 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q130. A bylaw amendment our stockholders adopted under (b)(3): the board may not further amend it.
#ASSERT `Is our board barred from further amending a bylaw amendment our stockholders adopted under section 203(b)(3)` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is our board barred from further amending a bylaw amendment our stockholders adopted under section 203(b)(3)` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q131. A corporation with no class listed on an exchange and 100 holders of record of its largest class: outside section 203.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation outside section 203 because it has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` FALSE FALSE 100 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A class listed on a national securities exchange, and the listing is not the result of an interested stockholder's action: not outside it.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation outside section 203 because it has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` TRUE FALSE 100 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The listing results from an interested stockholder's action: the "unless" clause disregards it, so the corporation is still outside section 203.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation outside section 203 because it has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` TRUE TRUE 100 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 2,000 holders of record: not "more than 2,000", so outside.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation outside section 203 because it has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` FALSE FALSE 2000 FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 2,001 holders of record: not outside.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation outside section 203 because it has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` FALSE FALSE 2001 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- 2,001 holders, and that number results from an interested stockholder's action: disregarded, so outside.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation outside section 203 because it has no listed or widely held class of voting stock` FALSE FALSE 2001 TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- Q132. I became an interested stockholder inadvertently, divested myself as soon as practicable, and but for the inadvertent acquisition I would not have been one within the 3 years: the restrictions do not apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder inadvertently` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- I did not divest as soon as practicable: they apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder inadvertently` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- I would have been an interested stockholder in the 3 years anyway: they apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder inadvertently` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- It was not inadvertent: they apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder inadvertently` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q133. A merger (a stockholder vote is required), proposed on 1 Jun 2026 after its announcement on 1 May 2026 and before consummation, with a person who was not an interested stockholder in the previous 3 years; 3 of the 5 continuing directors approved it: the restrictions do not apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only 2 of the 5 approved or did not oppose: not a majority.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 of 4 is exactly half, not a majority.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 4 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 of 4 is a majority.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 4 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The business combination is proposed on 1 Apr 2026, before the announcement of 1 May: too early.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The notice (10 Apr) came before the announcement (1 May): the earlier date governs, so a proposal on 15 Apr is in time.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 4 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 4 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The business combination is proposed on 1 May 2026, the very day of the announcement: "subsequent to" the announcement means after it, so not yet in time.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither a public announcement nor a notice has been made: there is no earlier date for the proposal to follow.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The transaction was consummated on 15 May; a business combination proposed on 1 Jun is after it: too late.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The person was an interested stockholder within the previous 3 years, and became one without the board's approval or in the (b)(7) period: no.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same person became one with the board's approval: yes.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A merger for which no stockholder vote is required under section 251(f): not one of the transactions listed.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A sale of assets worth $50 of a consolidated $100 (50%): a listed transaction.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a sale or other disposition of assets, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 50 100 1000 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Worth $49, below 50% of the consolidated assets ($100) and of the outstanding stock ($1,000): not listed.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a sale or other disposition of assets, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 49 100 1000 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Worth $500 of an outstanding stock worth $1,000 (50%), though only 5% of the consolidated assets of $10,000: "either" is enough, so listed.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a sale or other disposition of assets, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 500 10000 1000 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A disposition of the same size to a wholly-owned subsidiary: excluded.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a sale or other disposition of assets, as proposed` FALSE TRUE 50 100 1000 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A tender offer for 50 of the 100 votes outstanding: a listed transaction.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a tender or exchange offer, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 50 100 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A tender offer for 49 of 100: not listed.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `a tender or exchange offer, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 49 100 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Some other transaction: not one of the three listed.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because of the proposal of the business combination` `another transaction, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Q134. A merger for which a stockholder vote is required: the corporation must give all interested stockholders 20 days' notice.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation give all interested stockholders notice of this proposed transaction` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- A merger needing no vote under 251(f): no notice required.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation give all interested stockholders notice of this proposed transaction` `a merger or consolidation of the corporation, as proposed` TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A sale of assets worth 50% of the consolidated assets: notice required.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation give all interested stockholders notice of this proposed transaction` `a sale or other disposition of assets, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 50 100 1000 EQUALS TRUE
-- A tender or exchange offer: the notice sentence names only clauses (x) and (y), so none is required.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation give all interested stockholders notice of this proposed transaction` `a tender or exchange offer, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- A smaller sale of assets: none required.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation give all interested stockholders notice of this proposed transaction` `a sale or other disposition of assets, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 49 100 1000 EQUALS FALSE

-- Q135. Notice given on 1 May 2026 and the transaction consummated on 21 May 2026, 20 days later: not less than 20 days.
#ASSERT `Was the notice given to the interested stockholders at least 20 days before the transaction was consummated` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 21) EQUALS TRUE
-- Consummated 19 days after notice: not enough.
#ASSERT `Was the notice given to the interested stockholders at least 20 days before the transaction was consummated` (YMD 2026 5 2) (YMD 2026 5 21) EQUALS FALSE

-- Q136. The restrictions did not apply when I became an interested stockholder by reason of (b)(1) to (4), and the certificate then contained no election to be governed: they still do not apply to me.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder when they did not apply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The certificate then contained an election to be governed: the paragraph does not apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder when they did not apply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The restrictions did apply when I became one: the paragraph does not apply.
#ASSERT `Do the restrictions in section 203 not apply because I became an interested stockholder when they did not apply` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q137. Our original certificate elected to be governed by section 203: the election applies to me.
#ASSERT `Does our corporation's election to be governed by section 203 apply to me as an interested stockholder` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Elected by a certificate amendment effective 1 Mar 2026; I became an interested stockholder on 2 Mar 2026: it applies to me.
#ASSERT `Does our corporation's election to be governed by section 203 apply to me as an interested stockholder` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS TRUE
-- I became one on 28 Feb 2026, before the amendment took effect: it does not restrict a business combination with me.
#ASSERT `Does our corporation's election to be governed by section 203 apply to me as an interested stockholder` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS FALSE
-- No election at all: nothing applies.
#ASSERT `Does our corporation's election to be governed by section 203 apply to me as an interested stockholder` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS FALSE


§ `Section 203(c): the defined terms`

-- Q138. An affiliate of a person is one that controls it, is controlled by it, or is under common control with it. I control the other person: I am its affiliate.
#ASSERT `Am I an affiliate of this person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The other person controls me: affiliate.
#ASSERT `Am I an affiliate of this person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- We are under common control: affiliate.
#ASSERT `Am I an affiliate of this person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- No control relation at all: not an affiliate.
#ASSERT `Am I an affiliate of this person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q139. I am a director of the entity: it is my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this entity my associate` TRUE 0 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I own 20 of the 100 votes of a class of its voting stock: 20% or more, so my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this entity my associate` FALSE 20 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I own 19 of 100: under 20%, and I am not a director, officer or partner: not my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this entity my associate` FALSE 19 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No votes in the class: no percentage to work out.
#ASSERT `Is this entity my associate` FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q140. A trust in which I have a 20% beneficial interest: my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this trust or estate my associate` 20 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A 19% interest and I am not trustee: not my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this trust or estate my associate` 19 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am its trustee: my associate, whatever my interest.
#ASSERT `Is this trust or estate my associate` 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q141. My brother, who has the same residence as I do: my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this relative or spouse my associate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A relative at a different residence: not my associate.
#ASSERT `Is this relative or spouse my associate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a relative or spouse: the item does not reach them.
#ASSERT `Is this relative or spouse my associate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Q142. A merger of the corporation with me: a business combination.
#ASSERT `Is this merger or consolidation a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A merger with a third company that I caused, as a result of which subsection (a) does not apply to the surviving entity: a business combination.
#ASSERT `Is this merger or consolidation a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A merger with a third company that I caused, but subsection (a) still applies to the survivor: not.
#ASSERT `Is this merger or consolidation a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A merger with a third company that I did not cause: not.
#ASSERT `Is this merger or consolidation a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a merger of the corporation or a majority-owned subsidiary: not.
#ASSERT `Is this merger or consolidation a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q143. A sale of assets to me worth 10 of 100 of the consolidated assets (10%): a business combination.
#ASSERT `Is this disposition of assets a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 100 1000 EQUALS TRUE
-- Worth 9 of 100 and 9 of 1,000 of stock: below 10% of both.
#ASSERT `Is this disposition of assets a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE TRUE FALSE 9 100 1000 EQUALS FALSE
-- Worth 100 of 5,000 of consolidated assets but 100 of 1,000 of the stock (10%): "either", so yes.
#ASSERT `Is this disposition of assets a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 5000 1000 EQUALS TRUE
-- A disposition made proportionately as a stockholder (a pro rata dividend in kind): excluded.
#ASSERT `Is this disposition of assets a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 100 1000 EQUALS FALSE
-- Not to or with me: not a business combination with me.
#ASSERT `Is this disposition of assets a business combination with me as the interested stockholder` TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 100 1000 EQUALS FALSE

-- Q144. An issuance of stock to me, none of the exceptions applying: a business combination.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Under convertible securities outstanding before I became an interested stockholder: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Under a section 251(g) merger: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A pro rata dividend that does not increase my proportionate share: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A pro rata dividend that increases my proportionate share: the proviso takes it back in.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- An exchange offer on the same terms to all holders, no increase: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- It issues no stock to me: not a business combination under this item.
#ASSERT `Is this issuance or transfer of stock to me a business combination` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q145. A transaction that increases my proportionate share, not within the two exceptions: a business combination.
#ASSERT `Is this transaction that increases my proportionate share of the stock a business combination` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The increase is an immaterial fractional-share adjustment: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is this transaction that increases my proportionate share of the stock a business combination` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The increase comes from a redemption I did not cause: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is this transaction that increases my proportionate share of the stock a business combination` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- It does not increase my proportionate share: not under this item.
#ASSERT `Is this transaction that increases my proportionate share of the stock a business combination` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q146. A loan through the corporation that is not pro rata and not one of the permitted items: a business combination.
#ASSERT `Is my receipt of this financial benefit a business combination` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Received proportionately as a stockholder: excepted.
#ASSERT `Is my receipt of this financial benefit a business combination` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Expressly permitted in (c)(3)(i) to (iv): excepted.
#ASSERT `Is my receipt of this financial benefit a business combination` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- I receive no benefit: not under this item.
#ASSERT `Is my receipt of this financial benefit a business combination` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- Q147. I have the power to direct the entity's management and policies: I have control.
#ASSERT `Do I have control of this entity` TRUE 0 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I have no such power but own 20 of its 100 votes: presumed to have control.
#ASSERT `Do I have control of this entity` FALSE 20 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 20 of 100 votes and I rebutted the presumption by a preponderance of the evidence: no control.
#ASSERT `Do I have control of this entity` FALSE 20 100 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 20 of 100 votes held in good faith as a nominee for owners who do not control, and no power to direct: the presumption does not apply, so no control.
#ASSERT `Do I have control of this entity` FALSE 20 100 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 19 of 100 votes and no power to direct: below the 20% presumption, so no control.
#ASSERT `Do I have control of this entity` FALSE 19 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Q148. I beneficially own 100 votes, have the right to acquire 10 from outstanding stock and 5 from unissued stock, have 30 tendered shares to my own offer accepted (20 more not yet accepted),
-- may vote 7 under an agreement, hold a revocable proxy for 50 (given to 12 solicited persons), and 3 under my agreement with another beneficial owner: 100 + 10 + 5 + 30 + 7 + 3 = 155.
#ASSERT `How many votes of the corporation's voting stock do I own` 100 10 5 20 30 7 50 12 3 EQUALS 155
-- The proxy was solicited from only 5 persons (fewer than 10): the 50 votes count too, 205.
#ASSERT `How many votes of the corporation's voting stock do I own` 100 10 5 20 30 7 50 5 3 EQUALS 205
-- Exactly 10 persons solicited: "10 or more", so the proxy votes do not count.
#ASSERT `How many votes of the corporation's voting stock do I own` 100 10 5 20 30 7 50 10 3 EQUALS 155

-- Q149. I beneficially own 150 of 1,000 votes outstanding and nothing else: 15%, so an interested stockholder.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 150 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 149 of 1,000: under 15%.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 149 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 100 beneficially owned plus a right to 60 unissued votes: I own 160, and the unissued 60 count in the votes outstanding too (deemed owned), so 160 of 1,060 is 15.09%.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 100 0 60 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- With a right to only 50 unissued votes: 150 of 1,050 is 14.29%.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 100 0 50 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I am the corporation itself with 15%: the term excludes the corporation.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 150 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Limb (ii): I own only 10%, but I am an affiliate of the corporation and owned 15% or more within the last 3 years.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 100 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I own 10% and am an affiliate of an interested stockholder: "and the affiliates and associates of such person".
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 100 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Grandfathered: I owned shares in excess of 15% on 23 Dec 1987 and continued to own more than 15%: excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Acquired under a tender offer that commenced on 22 Dec 1987 (prior to 23 Dec 1987), and I continued to own more than 15%: excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 1987 12 22) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The tender offer commenced on 23 Dec 1987 itself: not "prior to" that day, so not excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 1987 12 23) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Acquired under an exchange offer announced on 1 Dec 1987 and commenced on 22 Mar 1988, the 90th day after 23 Dec 1987: excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) TRUE (YMD 1987 12 1) (YMD 1988 3 22) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same exchange offer commenced on 23 Mar 1988, the 91st day: not excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) TRUE (YMD 1987 12 1) (YMD 1988 3 23) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I got the shares from such a person by gift or inheritance: excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- My holding over 15% results solely from the corporation's action (a buy-back): excluded.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, but I later acquired more shares other than by further corporate action not caused by me: an interested stockholder again.
#ASSERT `Am I an interested stockholder of the corporation` 1000 200 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE (YMD 1987 1 1) (YMD 1987 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q150. A natural person is a person for section 203.
#ASSERT `Is the kind of entity a person for section 203` `a natural person` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the kind of entity a person for section 203` (`a corporation` OF `a stock corporation`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the kind of entity a person for section 203` `a general partnership` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the kind of entity a person for section 203` `a limited liability company` EQUALS TRUE
-- A statutory trust is an "other entity".
#ASSERT `Is the kind of entity a person for section 203` `a statutory trust` EQUALS TRUE

-- Q151. A corporation's capital stock is stock.
#ASSERT `Is this interest stock for section 203` (`a corporation` OF `a stock corporation`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An equity interest in a corporation that is not capital stock: for a corporation, "stock" means capital stock, so it is not stock.
#ASSERT `Is this interest stock for section 203` (`a corporation` OF `a stock corporation`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An equity interest in a limited liability company is stock.
#ASSERT `Is this interest stock for section 203` `a limited liability company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q152. Stock of a corporation entitled to vote generally in the election of directors is voting stock.
#ASSERT `Is this interest voting stock for section 203` (`a corporation` OF `a stock corporation`) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Stock of a corporation not entitled to vote generally in the election of directors is not.
#ASSERT `Is this interest voting stock for section 203` (`a corporation` OF `a stock corporation`) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An equity interest in a limited liability company entitled to vote generally in the election of its governing body is voting stock.
#ASSERT `Is this interest voting stock for section 203` `a limited liability company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Q153. 15 of 100 votes is 15%.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the voting stock do these votes represent` 15 100 EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `What percentage of the voting stock do these votes represent` 1 4 EQUALS JUST 25
-- No votes at all in the voting stock: no percentage.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the voting stock do these votes represent` 15 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q154. Our bylaw requires 75% where the section specifies 66 2/3%: it requires a greater vote, which subsection (d) forbids.
#ASSERT `Does our provision require a greater vote than section 203 specifies` 75 TRUE ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A provision requiring exactly 66 2/3%: the same vote, not a greater.
#ASSERT `Does our provision require a greater vote than section 203 specifies` ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) FALSE ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A provision requiring more than 66 2/3% (an extra vote above the same proportion): greater.
#ASSERT `Does our provision require a greater vote than section 203 specifies` ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) TRUE ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A provision requiring at least 50% where the section needs more than 50%: lesser.
#ASSERT `Does our provision require a greater vote than section 203 specifies` 50 FALSE 50 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Q155. A dispute under section 203 before the Court of Chancery: it has exclusive jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Does the court have jurisdiction to hear and determine the matter` `the Court of Chancery` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same dispute before the Superior Court: the Court of Chancery's jurisdiction is exclusive, so the Superior Court has none.
#ASSERT `Does the court have jurisdiction to hear and determine the matter` (`another party named in the provision` OF "the Superior Court") TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A matter that does not concern section 203: the subsection does not speak to it.
#ASSERT `Does the court have jurisdiction to hear and determine the matter` `the Court of Chancery` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Section 203 as a whole: may the corporation engage in this business combination?`

-- Q156. One public-company situation, varied one fact at a time.
-- THE BASE CASE. I am a director of a corporation with a class of voting stock listed on a national securities exchange (5,000 holders of record).
-- A stockholder became an interested stockholder on 1 Jan 2026, owning 20 of the 100 votes; a business combination with it is set for 1 Jun 2027. The board approved nothing beforehand,
-- no stockholder vote has been taken, the original certificate has no opt-out, no stockholder election has been made, and nothing in paragraphs (b)(5) to (b)(7) applies.
-- Every scenario below changes the named facts and leaves the rest as in the base case. The corporation is barred where the answer is JUST TRUE.
-- The base case: barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in this business combination with the interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 FALSE FALSE (YMD 1988 3 1) FALSE `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 0 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another transaction, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 100 (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The business combination is on 1 Jan 2029, the last day of the 3 years: still barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in this business combination with the interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 1) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 FALSE FALSE (YMD 1988 3 1) FALSE `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 0 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another transaction, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 100 (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On 2 Jan 2029, after the 3 years: not barred.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in this business combination with the interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2029 1 2) FALSE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 FALSE FALSE (YMD 1988 3 1) FALSE `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 0 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another transaction, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 100 (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board approved the business combination before the stockholder became interested: subsection (a)(1) frees it.
#ASSERT `Is our corporation barred from engaging in this business combination with the interested stockholder` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) TRUE FALSE 20 100 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 80 FALSE FALSE (YMD 1988 3 1) FALSE `the certificate of incorporation under s 203(b)(3)` 0 100 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE FALSE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another transaction, as proposed` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 0 100 (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board approved the transaction that made the stockholder interested, before it did so: (a)(1) frees it.
